{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>One who strikes a man and he dies shall surely be put to death.</b> After he completed the law of the Hebrew slave, with which he began, corresponding to the first commandment in the first tablet, he now begins with the law of murder, corresponding to the first commandment in the second tablet. And because there He warned but did not specify the punishment, he now comes and explains the punishment, saying: <b>מכה איש ומת מות יומת</b> — and this is in the case of intentional killing."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:02:19.841198306Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}